Z||000007||StuGood||12-29-2000||03:45 PM||||More playing around.  Here's the 1986 Fiero SE V6 Automatic.  Not sure if it converted very well..<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1986_FieroSE_V6_Auto.jpg"> <P>BTW, Cliff, everytime I click the "Post It!" button, doesn't that use up some of your available memory?  Is there a way for me to erase (or overwrite) images I've already posted?  Maybe I shouldn't be playing around with this so much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">    ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Seanh||12-30-2000||05:35 PM||||I was thinking of that also. I wish there was some way for us to delete files we have uploaded and dont need anymore. Making some way to do that is probally more trouble then its worth, but if its not too much trouble then it would be a good idea.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||12-30-2000||07:25 PM||||Yes, every time you click the "Post It!" button, you actually store an image on my server. Even if you post the same picture twice, <B>two</B> copies are stored (the second is automatically renamed).<P>At this moment, there are 4,666 images uploaded (totalling 281Mb) - making it the largest collection of Fiero-related images in the world.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
